<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Takamatsu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Takamatsu is a port city on the Seto Inland Sea, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagawa-prefecture">Kagawa Prefecture</a> on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. It grew around a sea castle begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikoma-chikamasa">Ikoma Chikamasa</a> in 1588, whose moats were fed by seawater, and was the seat of the Matsudaira lords of the Takamatsu Domain during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a>. It is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ritsurin-garden">Ritsurin Garden</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/takamatsu.jpg" alt="Takamatsu" width="320" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dokudami · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanazyukai20220729_7a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
